<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ice hockey world championship</p>
<p>final standings after the last round of the preliminary groups</p>
<p>on Saturday:</p>
<p>Group A, in Helsinki:</p>
<p>			     P   W   D   L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> 1. Czech Republic     5   4   0   1  18   9    8</p>
<p> 2. Finland		5   4   0   1  25   9    8</p>
<p> 3. Russia		 5   3   1   1  19  16    7</p>
<p> 4. Slovakia	     5   1   1   3  10  14    3</p>
<p> 5. France		 5   1   0   4  13  26    2</p>
<p> 6. Germany		5   1   0   4   4  15    2</p>
<p>The Czech Republic finished ahead of Finland, and France</p>
<p>ahead of Germany despite weaker goal differences since the</p>
<p>Czechs beat Finland and France beat Germany.</p>
<p>Group B, in Turku:</p>
<p>			     P   W   D   L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> 1. Sweden		 5   4   1   0  20   8    9</p>
<p> 2. Canada		 5   3   1   1  23  11    7</p>
<p> 3. U.S.		   5   3   0   2  14  15    6</p>
<p> 4. Latvia		 5   1   2   2  18  17    4</p>
<p> 5. Italy		  5   1   1   3  12  21    3</p>
<p> 6. Norway		 5   0   1   4   7  22    1</p>
<p>Top three teams from each group qualify for the medal</p>
<p>series. Teams four to six from both groups will meet in the</p>
<p>relegation series.</p>
</text>
